section.animate-in.space-y-3
	a.text-sm.nav-link.inline-flex.items-center.gap-1(href="/examples/tron") ← TRON examples
	h1.text-4xl.font-bold.tracking-tight.leading-none
		GradientText API-mode form
	p.max-w-prose.leading-relaxed(class="text-fg-muted")
		| The same
		code Form
		| /
		code Field
		| markup as the Notes example, but with a
		code submit
		| prop: the fields are posted as TRON to
		code POST /api/notes
		| through
		code api.post()
		| instead of a form action. Validation runs once, in the route — a 400 with
		code issues
		| lands on the matching Field.

section.animate-in-delayed.pt-8
	.grid.gap-6(class="md:grid-cols-2")
		Card
			+snippet('header')
				h3.text-base.font-semibold Create a note
			Form(submit!="{createNote}" onsuccess!="{onCreated}" bind:submitting!="{submitting}" resetOnSuccess!="{true}")
				Field(label="Title" name="title" required)
					Input(name="title" placeholder="leave empty to see a server-side validation error")
				Field(label="Body" name="body" help="Optional")
					Textarea(name="body" placeholder="body (optional)…" rows="3")
				Btn(type="submit" variant="primary" icon="lucide:send" loading!="{submitting}") Create via API
		Card
			+snippet('header')
				h3.text-base.font-semibold Created this session
			+if('created.length === 0')
				p.text-sm(class="text-fg-muted") Nothing yet.
			+else
				ul.space-y-1.text-sm
					+each('created as n (n.id)')
						li
							a.nav-link(href!="/examples/norns/notes/{n.id}") {n.title}
							span.text-xs.ml-2(class="text-fg-subtle") id {n.id}

section.pt-10.space-y-2
	h2.text-lg.font-semibold What to look at
	ul.list-disc.pl-5.space-y-1.text-sm(class="text-fg-muted")
		li
			| Submit with an empty title: the route throws
			code error(400, issues)
			| , the client surfaces it as
			code ApiError.body.issues
			| , and Form feeds those issues into the same context the action path uses.
		li
			| Small bodies go out as plain JSON under the
			code application/tron
			| content type (valid TRON); the route reads both through the serializer's
			code parseBody
			| .
		li
			| Form actions still work unchanged — SvelteKit only dispatches form-encoded POSTs to them, which is why JSON / TRON clients target a
			code +server.c
			| route.

<script>
	import { toast } from '@human-synthesis/norns-ui/toast'
	import { createNote } from '$lib/norns/notes/client/api'

	submitting .= $state false
	created .= $state []

	onCreated := (result, values) =>
		created = [{ id: result.id, title: String(values.title) }, ...created]
		toast `Created note ${result.id}`, { variant: 'success' }
</script>
